The Hateno Ancient Tech Lab is located on a hill on the northeastern end of [[Hateno Village]], overlooking the [[Necluda Sea]]. It is a three-story tower, with the main Lab taking up the first floor. The second floor consists of [[Symin]]'s room, while [[Purah's Room]] is located on the third floor. The remains of a [[Guardian Stalker]] are strapped down to the roof. Several [[Sign]]s leading to the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab warn against visitors and suggest caution.<ref>{{Cite|{{Icon|BotW Arrow Up}} Hateno Ancient Tech Lab<br/>NO SOLICITING|Sign|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Hateno Ancient Tech Lab {{Icon|BotW Arrow Right}}<br/>Mind the lanterns!|Sign|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Hateno Ancient Tech Lab {{Icon|BotW Arrow Right}}<br/>Enter at your own risk!|Sign|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|- Hateno Ancient Tech Lab -<br/>If the flame is blue, the furnace is hot! DO NOT TOUCH!|Sign|BotW}}</ref> The Lab is one of two successors to the [[Ancient Research Institute]], the other being the [[Akkala Ancient Tech Lab]].

Following the second [[Great Calamity]], a source of [[Ancient Energy]] was found in [[Necluda]].<ref>{{Cite|We found large amounts of ancient energy in the Necluda and Akkala regions. We could continue our research.|Robbie's Memoirs|BotW}}</ref> After playing rock, paper, scissors with [[Robbie]], it was decided that [[Purah]] would continue her research in Hateno Village.<ref>{{Cite|Just as we had in Hyrule Castle, we could again set ourselves to finding some way to seal Calamity Ganon away. We decided who would go where in the only fair way: rock, paper, scissors. I set out for Akkala soon after.|Robbie's Memoirs|BotW}}</ref> At Purah's insistence, Robbie escorted her there, carrying her [[Guidance Stone]] in a cart.<ref>{{Cite|I was all set to go to Akkala, but first I decided to go with Dr. Purah to the ancient energy source in Necluda. ...Actually, that implies I had any choice. Dr. Purah laid on a pretty heavy guilt trip when I suggested her going alone. "In a world as dangerous as ours, are you seriously asking me to travel alone?" She's so darned pushy... Anyway, Dr. Purah promised Lady Impa that they'd meet again someday, then she and I set out from Kakariko Village... But not before loading a cart with the Guidance Stone Dr. Purah had been using at Hyrule Castle.|Robbie's Memoirs|BotW}}</ref> However, the pair became separated at [[Fort Hateno]], and Purah continued on her own.<ref>{{Cite|Lost in my thoughts, I didn't notice that Dr. Purah had slipped away. I knew Hateno Village wasn't much farther along the road, and that the Calamity had barely touched that area... So I felt safe letting her continue on her own. We parted ways without even saying good-bye, I suppose.|Robbie's Memoirs|BotW}}</ref> Purah's research at the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab focuses on the [[Sheikah Slate]] and its [[Rune]]s.<ref name="Nanna">{{Cite|[Your mentor?] My mentor used to work closely with Princess Zelda in her research of that {{Color BotW|Blue|Sheikah Slate}}. Go to the research facility in Hateno Village, located to the far east of here. However... Um... Just know that this mentor of mine is...a bit odd.|Nanna|BotW}}</ref> The Lab also boasts a collection of all known [[Book]]s on ancient civilizations.<ref>{{Cite|I imagine you've never seen so many books in one place. Pretty incredible, isn't it? We've gathered all of Hyrule's known literature on ancient civilizations here.|Symin|BotW}}</ref> Two of these Books are the ''[[Camera Manual]]'', ''[[Sheikah Sensor Notes]]'', and ''[[Sheikah Slate Manual]]'', all of which were written by Purah and Symin.<ref>{{Cite|Camera Manual<br/>Written by: Purah!|Camera Manual|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Sheikah Sensor Notes<br/>Author: Symin|Sheikah Sensor Notes|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Sheikah Slate Manual<br/>Written by: Purah!|Sheikah Slate Manual|BotW}}</ref>

Over the years, three research assistants are known to have resided at the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab with Purah. The first is [[Nanna]], who describes Purah as having a strange personality.<ref name="Nanna"/> The next known assistant is [[Jerrin]], who was later sent to the Akkala Ancient Tech Lab by [[Impa]].<ref>{{Cite|I would have been lost in my work even then... But around that time, a young woman named Jerrin arrived. She'd first trained with Dr. Purah, then Lady Impa had sent her to aid me. She quickly proved herself quite capable.|Robbie's Memoirs|BotW}}</ref> Finally, Purah's current assistant is Symin, and while he struggles with the disorganized state that Purah keeps the Lab in, he is still honored to work with her.<ref>{{Cite|I have the utmost respect for Ms. Purah and all she's accomplished. I'm honored to be her assistant.|Symin|BotW}}</ref><ref name="CaC 271">{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 271}}</ref>

Sometime prior to [[Link]]'s arrival at the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab, Purah began development of an anti-aging Rune.<ref>{{Cite|Research diary for anti-aging rune. CLASSIFIED! For Purah's eyes only!|Purah's Diary|BotW}}</ref> Her goal was to reverse the aging process, bringing older warriors out of retirement to fight [[Calamity Ganon]] upon his return.<ref>{{Cite|Date: ??? Work has finally begun on my anti-aging rune. If all goes to plan, I believe it will effectively reverse the aging process. This technology will enable us to make retired warriors young again, thereby strengthening the Hyrulean army. When Calamity Ganon inevitably returns, we'll be ready. Our offense will be solid, and our defense impenetrable. The need for this tech pains me, but I truly hope to use it to attain everlasting peace for all.|Purah's Diary|BotW}}</ref> Purah tested the Rune on her, and over time, she regressed to the age of six.<ref>{{Cite|Date: ??? The beta version of my anti-aging rune is complete. I have already added it to the Sheikah Slate I made for myself. Since I am to be the test subject of this experiment, Symin booted up the rune and directed its rays at my body. After 20 seconds of exposure, I felt extreme fatigue and broke into a fever, forcing us to cease the experiment. Unable to stay awake, I went to bed immediately. Tomorrow I will try to figure out what went awry.|Purah's Diary|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Anti-Aging Experimental Trial<br/>Day 7<br/>This morning's exam results indicated that I am still age 6, same as yesterday. Perhaps my age-reversal has stopped.|Purah's Diary|BotW}}</ref> Once she developed an age-boosting Rune to reverse its effects, though, she discovered that the [[Furnace]]'s [[Blue Flame]] had been extinguished, thereby deactivating her Guidance Stone.<ref>{{Cite|As luck would have it, today I also finished developing the beta version of an age-boosting rune! ♪ If successful, this should be able to reverse the effects of the anti-aging rune. I hope it will, anyway. All I need to do is increase the output and expose myself to its rays...However, when I tried to add this feature to the Sheikah Slate I made, I found that the Guidance Stone had stopped! What's more, the blue flame in the furnace outside has gone out!|Purah's Diary|BotW}}</ref> Symin attempted to retrieve the Blue Flame from the [[Ancient Furnace]], but a combination of his clumsiness and [[Rain]] caused him to fail.<ref>{{Cite|I sent Symin to the ancient furnace, but he was too clumsy and it was raining and nothing went to plan.|Purah's Diary|BotW}}</ref> When Purah herself tried to go, she was seen by [[Karin]].<ref>{{Cite|So I had to go down there to help, but a girl in the village saw me. What a mess I've made...|Purah's Diary|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|There's a {{Color BotW|Red|girl}} staying up at the {{Color BotW|Blue|Hateno Ancient Tech Lab}}. I saw her come outside! She was right over there! It's true!|Karin|BotW}}</ref> As a result of this, Purah has not left the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab, and the residents of Hateno Village have not seen her.<ref>{{Cite|Can old-woman Purah not get around on her own anymore? Is she making the youth carry things around for her? I haven't seen Purah lately... I wonder if those rumors are true...|Leop|BotW}}</ref>

As part of the "[[Locked Mementos]]" [[Main Quest]], Impa sends Link to the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab to repair his Sheikah Slate.<ref>{{Cite|...It seems to me that your {{Color BotW|Blue|Sheikah Slate}} is not yet complete. The device Princess Zelda left you is your guide and also your memory. Now, let's see... Someone at the {{Color BotW|Red|research lab in Hateno Village}} might be able to help you...|Impa|BotW}}</ref> When Link first speaks to Purah, she points him towards Symin, who she claims is the director.<ref>{{Cite|The {{Color BotW|Red|director}} is in the back. A terribly busy person, that one. Please try to keep it brief.|Purah|BotW}}</ref> However, Symin reveals that Purah is actually the Lab's director, despite her youthful appearance.<ref>{{Cite|Oh, that's right... I haven't introduced our {{Color BotW|Red|director}}. Ms. Purah happens to be right over there... As the {{Color BotW|Blue|Hateno Ancient Tech Lab}} {{Color BotW|Red|director}}, Ms. Purah is the world's foremost authority on ancient Hyrule culture.|Symin|BotW}}</ref> Before repairing the Sheikah Slate, Purah asks Link to retrieve the Blue Flame from the Ancient Furnace, which will reactivate her Guidance Stone and allow her to restore the missing Runes.<ref>{{Cite|Let me explain what this errand details. You know the unlit {{Color BotW|Blue|furnace}} on the wall just outside this laboratory? Could you please bring the {{Color BotW|Blue|blue flame}} from the {{Color BotW|Blue|ancient furnace}} in town? Oh, and also use it to light our {{Color BotW|Blue|furnace}}? This sweet little {{Color BotW|Blue|Guidance Stone}} will start working once you do that, allowing us to restore your missing {{Color BotW|Red|runes}}!|Purah|BotW}}</ref> When he does this, the [[Travel Gate]] outside of the Lab will activate, allowing Link to [[Warping|Warp]] to it.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Hateno Ancient Tech Lab is now set as a travel gate.}}|N/A|BotW}}</ref> Afterwards, Purah will use the Guidance Stone to repair the [[Camera]], [[Hyrule Compendium]], and [[Album]].<ref>{{Cite|Hokay then, {{Color BotW|Blue|Sheikah Slate}} repair... underway! {{Color BotW|Blue|Guidance Stone}} lock removed! Now...let's do this thing!|Purah|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Sheikah Slate authenticated. Camera, Hyrule Compendium, and album missing files confirmed.}}|Guidance Stone|BotW}}</ref> After discovering that there are old [[Picture]]s in the Album, Purah sends Link back to Impa to learn about them.<ref>{{Cite|Hmmm... Ah, it's not just a pretty girl in these images. Yes, there are also some {{Color BotW|Red|old landscape photos}} stored in the {{Color BotW|Blue|album}}. I knew Princess Zelda had made frequent use of the {{Color BotW|Blue|Camera}} feature, but this... Hey, Linky! It dawns on me that you were Princess Zelda's appointed knight, which means... there's a strong possibility that you {{Color BotW|Red|accompanied}} her to all of the {{Color BotW|Red|places where these pictures were taken}}. Oh...right. The "lost memory" thing could prove troublesome. But don't lose hope! It just means these pictures could be the missing piece to help restore your lost memories! If my hunch is correct, I suggest you check in with {{Color BotW|Red|Impa}}. She knows more about Princess Zelda than even I do!|Purah|BotW}}</ref> She also mentions wanting Link to bring either her or Robbie [[Ancient Material]]s, which begins the "[[Slated for Upgrades]]" and "[[Robbie's Research]]" [[Side Quest]]s.<ref>{{Cite|Oh, yeah! There's just one more thing I need from you! You don't have to worry about this until after you see Impa, but I want you to bring me back some {{Color BotW|Red|ancient materials}}! Bring them either to {{Color BotW|Red|me}} or to {{Color BotW|Red|Robbie}} at the {{Color BotW|Red|Akkala Ancient Tech Lab}}. As if my joy weren't enough, if you bring us {{Color BotW|Red|ancient materials}}, we'll give you {{Color BotW|Red|something good}} as a reward.|Purah|BotW}}</ref>

[[File:BotW Slated for Upgrades.png|thumb|left|250px|Link upgrading his Sheikah Slate]]
During "Slated for Upgrades," Purah explains that she will power up Link's Runes in exchanged for Ancient Materials.<ref>{{Cite|[Something good?] Aha! I'm glad you asked! If you bring me some {{Color BotW|Red|ancient materials}}, I'll {{Color BotW|Red|power up}} your {{Color BotW|Blue|runes}}!|Purah|BotW}}</ref> It costs three [[Ancient Screw]]s to upgrade the [[Sheikah Sensor]],<ref>{{Cite|You'll need {{Color BotW|Red|three ancient screws}} to power up your {{Color BotW|Blue|Sheikah Sensor}}.|Purah|BotW}}</ref> three [[Ancient Shaft]]s to upgrade the [[Remote Bomb]]s,<ref>{{Cite|You'll need {{Color BotW|Red|three ancient shafts}} to power up your {{Color BotW|Blue|Remote Bombs}}.|Purah|BotW}}</ref> and three [[Ancient Core]]s to upgrade [[Stasis]].<ref>{{Cite|You'll need {{Color BotW|Red|three ancient cores}} to power up {{Color BotW|Blue|Stasis}}.|Purah|BotW}}</ref> Once Link provides the necessary Ancient Materials, Purah will use the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab's Guidance Stone to enhance a Rune of his choice.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Sheikah Slate authenticated. Enhancing Sheikah Sensor.}}|Guidance Stone|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Sheikah Slate authenticated. Enhancing Remote Bomb rune.}}|Guidance Stone|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Sheikah Slate authenticated. Enhancing Stasis rune.}}|Guidance Stone|BotW}}</ref>

After Link upgrades his Sheikah Sensor, Symin will ask to see it.<ref>{{Cite|Oooh! The {{Color BotW|Blue|Sheikah Sensor +}}! I reaaally want to see it...|Symin|BotW}}</ref> When Link approaches him, he will suggest testing it out for themselves.<ref>{{Cite|You've acquired the {{Color BotW|Blue|Sheikah Sensor +}}! That should really come in handy. With that, you can sense things that you've captured with your {{Color BotW|Blue|Camera}}. Explaining won't do it justice—why not learn by trying? Let's give it a shot, so to speak.|Symin|BotW}}</ref> To do this, he tells Link to take a Picture of a [[Sunshroom]], which can be found behind the Hateno Ancient Tech Lab.<ref>{{Cite|Let's see here. First, go take a picture of a {{Color BotW|Blue|sunshroom}} with the {{Color BotW|Blue|Camera}}. There is one {{Color BotW|Red|behind}} the lab.|Symin|BotW}}</ref> Afterwards, the "[[Sunshroom Sensing]]" Side Quest will begin. Once Link has returned with the Picture, Symin explains that he can use the Sheikah Sensor to sense Sunshrooms, since one has been registered in his Hyrule Compendium.<ref>{{Cite|It seems like you got a picture of a {{Color BotW|Blue|sunshroom}}! Excellent. Next, open your {{Color BotW|Blue|Hyrule Compendium}} and tune the sensor to your {{Color BotW|Blue|picture}} of the {{Color BotW|Blue|sunshroom}}. The {{Color BotW|Blue|Sheikah Sensor +}} will then be able to sense {{Color BotW|Blue|sunshrooms}}!|Symin|BotW}}</ref> To learn more, he suggests reading the ''Sheikah Sensor Notes'' nearby.<ref>{{Cite|The detailed instructions are written down in the {{Color BotW|Blue|book}} on the desk there. You should read them.|Symin|BotW}}</ref> Next, Symin tasks Link with finding three Sunshrooms using the Sheikah Sensor.<ref>{{Cite|This seems like a nice opportunity to ask if you'd mind bringing me {{Color BotW|Red|three sunshrooms}}. You can find {{Color BotW|Red|sunshrooms}} growing in {{Color BotW|Red|Retsam Forest}}, I believe... The {{Color BotW|Blue|Sheikah Sensor +}} should make it a snap!|Symin|BotW}}</ref> When Link brings the Sunshrooms to Symin, he will give him three [[Hearty Truffle]]s as a reward.<ref>{{Cite|Thank you. Here you go.|Symin|BotW}}</ref>

Following this Side Quest, Symin will begin to sell Hyrule Compendium entries to Link.<ref>{{Cite|These are the {{Color BotW|Blue|pictures}} you can currently add.|Symin|BotW}}</ref> Link has the options to buy [[Fauna Picture]]s,<ref>{{Cite|Sure, I can sell you come {{Color BotW|Blue|fauna pictures}}. How many would you like?|Symin|BotW}}</ref> [[Enemy Picture]]s,<ref>{{Cite|Sure, I can sell you come {{Color BotW|Blue|enemy pictures}}. How many would you like?|Symin|BotW}}</ref> [[Material Picture]]s,<ref>{{Cite|Sure, I can sell you come {{Color BotW|Blue|material pictures}}. How many would you like?|Symin|BotW}}</ref> [[Weapon Picture]]s,<ref>{{Cite|Sure, I can sell you come {{Color BotW|Blue|weapon pictures}}. How many would you like?|Symin|BotW}}</ref> and [[Other Picture]]s.<ref>{{Cite|Sure, I can sell you come {{Color BotW|Blue|other pictures}}. How many would you like?|Symin|BotW}}</ref> Each Picture costs 100 [[Rupee]]s.<ref>{{Cite|You want 1 of the {{Color BotW|Blue|fauna pictures}}? That will be {{Color BotW|Red|100 rupees}}.|Symin|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|You want 1 of the {{Color BotW|Blue|enemy pictures}}? That will be {{Color BotW|Red|100 rupees}}.|Symin|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|You want 1 of the {{Color BotW|Blue|material pictures}}? That will be {{Color BotW|Red|100 rupees}}.|Symin|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|You want 1 of the {{Color BotW|Blue|weapon pictures}}? That will be {{Color BotW|Red|100 rupees}}.|Symin|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|You want 1 of the {{Color BotW|Blue|other pictures}}? That will be {{Color BotW|Red|100 rupees}}.|Symin|BotW}}</ref> After Link defeats [[Dark Beast Ganon]], [[Elite Enemy Picture]]s will become available, costing 500 [[Rupee]]s.<ref>{{Cite|Sure, I can sell you come {{Color BotW|Blue|elite enemy pictures}}. How many would you like?|Symin|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|You want 1 of the {{Color BotW|Blue|elite enemy pictures}}? That will be {{Color BotW|Red|500 rupees}}.|Symin|BotW}}</ref> Once Link makes a purchase, the Hyrule Compendium will be updated with the Pictures.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|Hyrule Compendium updated.}}|Sheikah Slate|BotW}}</ref> Symin will then thank Link for supporting their research.<ref>{{Cite|Thank you for supporting our research.|Symin|BotW}}</ref>

